---
kind: lore
id: skerry.tornPage
title: The torn page
---

<beat id="pieceThePage" on="examine" target="item.torn_page" title="The burnt scraps" spentBy="holds('pieced', ['torn_page'])" when="holds('carrying', ['torn_page'])">
  @narrator: Seven scraps of the log's paper, browned at the edges. Ada tried to burn them and lost her nerve.
  <branch id="firstScrap" prompt="Which scrap begins the entry?">
    <choice id="aug" label="The one dated in August">
      @narrator: "Aug. 30th." The next scrap joins it along the tear, and the next. The page comes back in the keeper's hand.
      ::assert{pieced(torn_page)}
      ::assert{reported(gallery_rail)}
    </choice>
    <choice id="tell" label="The one with the word &quot;tell&quot;">
      @narrator: The tear does not match anything. You sweep the scraps back into the envelope.
    </choice>
    <choice id="stain" label="The one with the oil stain">
      @narrator: A corner, no words on it. It fits nowhere yet.
    </choice>
  </branch>
</beat>

<entry id="tornPageRead" on="examine" target="item.torn_page" category="note" title="30 August" when="holds('pieced', ['torn_page'])">
  @elias: Aug. 30th. Seaward rail rotten at both bolts. Wrote to the Board for a new one. Wrote again.
  @elias: If they will not pay, somebody tell them what it costs. Their answer is behind A.'s photograph.
</entry>

<entry id="boardLetter" on="examine" target="item.requisition" category="item" title="The Board's letter" once="run" when="holds('pieced', ['torn_page'])">
  @narrator: Behind the photograph over the stove, folded small: a letter on the Board's paper, dated 3rd September.
  @narrator: "The Board regrets that no funds can be allotted for the renewal of the gallery rail at Skerry Rock in the present year."
  ::assert{refusedRepair(gallery_rail)}
</entry>
